392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 72 0 R
/T (Each dilemma presents an everyday situation that invites children to reflect on what they would do and how their actions can affect others.  Each dilemma is presented with a short narrative, a central question, and associated values. These situations are designed to encourage reflection, storytelling, and digital creation through tools like Scratch. Each group can either work on the same dilemma or divide up the different proposed dilemmas, allowing for a richer collective reflection when sharing the various stories and perspectives.)
/E (Each dilemma presents an everyday situation that invites children to reflect on what they would do and how their actions can affect others.  Each dilemma is presented with a short narrative, a central question, and associated values. These situations are designed to encourage reflection, storytelling, and digital creation through tools like Scratch. Each group can either work on the same dilemma or divide up the different proposed dilemmas, allowing for a richer collective reflection when sharing the various stories and perspectives.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
